---
description: Avoid invalid dynamic request APIs inside cached Next.js provider code
globs:
  - "app/**/*.ts"
  - "app/**/*.tsx"
  - "components/**/*.ts"
  - "components/**/*.tsx"
  - "lib/**/*.ts"
  - "lib/**/*.tsx"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Next.js cache boundaries

This app uses Next.js App Router, React Server Components, Server Actions, and `"use cache"`.

When editing provider functions in `lib/nopcommerce`:

- Do not call `cookies()`, `headers()`, request-specific APIs, or other dynamic APIs inside functions marked `"use cache"`.
- Keep request-specific behavior in uncached functions or Server Actions.
- If a cached provider needs a request ID for outbound fetches, generate one locally instead of reading request headers.
- Keep provider fetch helpers safe for static generation, partial prerendering, and cached data reads.
- Run `pnpm prettier:check`, `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`, and `pnpm build` after changes touching cached provider code.
